From: pogo-bash <pogo-bash@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:47:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 53/56] LibWeb: pushState and replaceState pass their
 serialized data as the navigate event's classicHistoryAPIState

It went in the navigationAPIState slot, so the navigate event's hashChange was true for a pushState to a fragment (Chrome and the spec: false), and the entry's navigation API state was the classic state.
---
 Libraries/LibWeb/HTML/History.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Libraries/LibWeb/HTML/History.cpp b/Libraries/LibWeb/HTML/History.cpp
index 4878af1df3..60c2ef521b 100644
--- a/Libraries/LibWeb/HTML/History.cpp
+++ b/Libraries/LibWeb/HTML/History.cpp
@@ -215,7 +215,7 @@ WebIDL::ExceptionOr<void> History::shared_history_push_replace_state(JS::Realm&
     //    with navigationType set to historyHandling, isSameDocument set to true, destinationURL set to newURL,
     //    and classicHistoryAPIState set to serializedData.
     auto navigation_type = history_handling == HistoryHandlingBehavior::Push ? NavigationType::Push : NavigationType::Replace;
-    auto continue_ = navigation->fire_a_push_replace_reload_navigate_event(navigation_type, new_url, true, UserNavigationInvolvement::None, {}, {}, serialized_data);
+    auto continue_ = navigation->fire_a_push_replace_reload_navigate_event(navigation_type, new_url, true, UserNavigationInvolvement::None, {}, {}, {}, serialized_data);
     // 9. If continue is false, then return.
     if (!continue_)
         return {};
